# Netlify serves this site's HTML from its CDN. Without this, a browser can
# hold on to an old copy of index.html for a long time after a deploy — which
# is exactly how you end up testing a build you already replaced, and
# concluding the code is broken when it isn't.
#
# The page is a single self-contained file with the fonts and logo inlined,
# so there is nothing to gain from caching it and everything to lose.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
